# Every change requires review from a code owner (enforced by the main branch ruleset).
# Core FDE owns the plugin; Core owns the Doppel MCP server it points at. Security is a
# code owner of every path as well. An approval from a member of any one of the three
# teams satisfies the requirement.
*                       @doppelxyz/core-fde @doppelxyz/core @doppelxyz/security

# The MCP endpoint, the manifests, the security policy, and the repository
# configuration are security-relevant. They are listed by path so that their owners
# stay explicit if the default above changes.
/mcp.json               @doppelxyz/core-fde @doppelxyz/core @doppelxyz/security
/.mcp.json              @doppelxyz/core-fde @doppelxyz/core @doppelxyz/security
/plugin.json            @doppelxyz/core-fde @doppelxyz/core @doppelxyz/security
/.claude-plugin/        @doppelxyz/core-fde @doppelxyz/core @doppelxyz/security
/SECURITY.md            @doppelxyz/core-fde @doppelxyz/core @doppelxyz/security
/.github/               @doppelxyz/core-fde @doppelxyz/core @doppelxyz/security
